      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "A genus of medium-sized, crested passerines endemic to Australia, characterised by stout, wedge-shaped bills and loud, distinctive vocalisations. They are divided into two groups: the whipbirds, with a characteristic whip-crack song, and the wedgebills, with a softer, bubbling call. They inhabit dense undergrowth, where they forage on the ground for insects and seeds.",
